invariant: INV-16
file: tls.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_host
reason: the raw and ca ch_connect stops writing the answer the session's ch_cfg.cpu gives
  into its record directions, so each record it seals or opens runs
  Poly1305 under 0, the decomposition, whatever the value states. The key
  exchange and the signature still follow the bit, so only a count of the
  record's copy notices: test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h requires an end
  whose ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY to call no file
  under its own names.

--- old
#ifdef CH_CPU_RUNTIME
    tlsi_record_widemul(t);
#endif
    int rc = tlsi_epoch_init(t, cfg, psk_ok);
--- new
    int rc = tlsi_epoch_init(t, cfg, psk_ok);
